WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Tell me about the date.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- So let me tell you about the date.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.660
This was when I was in college.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:03.620
It was my senior year

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.890
going to Baylor University

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.080
in Waco, Texas--
- [Kelly] Oh, Baylor Bear.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.020
- I was a senior--
- Bear.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.800
- living by myself in an apartment,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.940
and people kinda knew my apartment.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.740
I'd been doing the ventriloquism forever.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.490
In fact my license plate
actually said dummy on my car.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.970
So people knew.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.429
So my apartment--

00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:21.179
- I see why you got all the ladies.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.170
- I admit that what I do
for a living is not normal,

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.003
and I get it.

00:00:27.003 --> 00:00:28.370
I don't know how I got the wife I have.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.490
Audrey and I have been
married for seven years now,

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.360
and she's beautiful,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.193
and it works,
- [Kelly] Super hot.

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:33.200
- and it's fantastic.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.826
But whether--
- See that probably

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:37.280
I shouldn't have said.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.170
But I did.
- That's okay.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.670
But never in the history of the planet

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.967
has any woman ever said,

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:42.730
"Ventriloquist. That's hot."

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.090
- Hey, no, you don't know that.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.030
- [Jeff] I do know that.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:46.863
- I don't know.

00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:47.908
- I do know.

00:00:47.908 --> 00:00:49.250
- Well, I've never heard of it.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.100
They never say that to me.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.300
Let me get to the story.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:53.760
So I'd been dating this girl,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.470
and my apartment was covered with dummies.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.840
They were my collection of dummies.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.130
I'm not getting rid of my damn dummies

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.730
'cause they didn't bring me joy.

00:01:02.436 --> 00:01:05.153
- You might have to say
goodbye to one dummy.

00:01:05.153 --> 00:01:06.006
Share the dummy.

00:01:06.006 --> 00:01:06.839
- [Kelly] They all spark joy.

00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:09.630
- I like my clutter of dolls.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.820
So anyway, the dummies are
lined up in the main room,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.320
the first room you walk
in in the apartment.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.720
They're all lined up and
sitting on the walls.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.590
It's kinda creepy when you walk in.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.471
- I mean, it kinda sounds
like a Dateline special,

00:01:17.471 --> 00:01:19.000
but that's fine.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.060
- Okay, but it was my thing,

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:21.480
and I built 'em, and I collected 'em.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.313
They were antiques.

00:01:22.313 --> 00:01:23.146
It was just weird.

00:01:23.146 --> 00:01:24.137
And people actually said to me,

00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:25.657
"Yeah, you gotta go to
Jeff Dunham's apartment.

00:01:25.657 --> 00:01:26.490
"That's a thing."

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.110
- Anyway, so this girl,
- Oh, I love it.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.950
- I'd only taken her
out three or four times,

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.930
so it was kinda, we were getting close.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.540
So I brought her over to the apartment,

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.690
and we're sitting on the couch,

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.490
and I had secretly,

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.507
this is the thing that's gonna come out,

00:01:40.507 --> 00:01:41.910
and the tape is there.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.330
I had secretly put a VHS recorder,

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.463
this was in the '80s, in the corner,

00:01:46.463 --> 00:01:50.520
and I hid the camera amongst the dummies,

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.949
and it was shooting the couch.

00:01:52.949 --> 00:01:54.310
- This did just become--
- Why?

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.360
- a Dateline special.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.350
- So here I am.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.697
James Taylor's playing--

00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:01.530
- [Beth] Good taste in music.
- on my stereo.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.620
- [Kelly] Okay, Casanova.
- Of course, yeah.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:04.910
- And we're getting kinda romantic,

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:06.250
and the tape is going,

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.570
and I did this for one reason only.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.660
I wanted to see her reaction

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.700
when the dummy that was in the corner

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.640
that I had secretly radio-controlled

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.440
moved when I wasn't looking and she was.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.267
So all those in the female audience going,

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.100
"Oh, you're horrible."

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.380
- No, you sound like my husband.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.820
He likes to scare people.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.240
- But it's the greatest tape ever

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.073
because here it is.

00:02:26.073 --> 00:02:27.480
I'm sitting here with her like this,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.750
and I'm looking over the other way,

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.650
and I had the radio control
under a pillow over here.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.483
So I moved it,

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:32.880
and the dummy moved his head and his eyes

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.983
just like this, and she's like,

00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:35.640
she had a great Texas accent.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.110
She's like, "Oh my God."

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.477
I'm like, "What?"

00:02:38.477 --> 00:02:39.310
"That dummy over there.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.027
"That dummy just moved its head."

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.390
And I'm like, "No, it didn't."

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.223
She goes, "It did.

00:02:45.223 --> 00:02:46.056
"I just saw him move."

00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:47.507
I'm like, "Yeah, everybody says that.

00:02:47.507 --> 00:02:48.660
"It's fine."

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.680
So I let another

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.590
five minutes pass,
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:51.900
- and it moves its eyes
and its head again.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.830
She goes, "Ho!"
- I'd have been out the door.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:53.663
- That's what she did.

00:02:53.663 --> 00:02:54.496
She was out the door.

00:02:54.496 --> 00:02:56.540
She's gone, and I'm like, "Oh yeah!"

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.373
The greatest tape ever.

00:02:57.373 --> 00:02:59.029
- It's like the greatest tape ever.

00:02:59.029 --> 00:03:00.112
That's wrong.

